s to being fearful despite his  outward appearance we were told this  would be the case by shinobu the  physical change had no impact we were  led to believe on his actual mind which  is still that of a kid so that will no  doubt lead to some hilarious situations  where an intimidating looking adult or  dragon will act in childish ways not  only will this be funny but it's better  for the story because momo is still  forced to overcome his fears rather than  flying past them with the power of a  magical fruit thus we get this funny  situation where the giant dragon is  scared of heights and talks about how  his body is frozen most likely because  he's so frightened momo even said that  raising his head alone in this form is  daunting because he's so big that line  definitely made me laugh luffy obviously  doesn't care calling him a wimp and  wonders how he's still scared of heights  if he's a grown-up but as i explained  he's not actually a grown-up except in  appearance of course momo does have his  pride and tells luffy to keep his  insolent thoughts to himself and that  samurai feared nothing that's what i'm  talking about love that line samurai  fear nothing we continue to get a back  and forth of luffy trying to get momo to  fly as fast as possible so he can meet  up with kaido again and momo telling him  to slow down and give him a second i  don't think momo will suddenly start  acting like a complete adult by the end  of this arc in humorous ways he'll  probably keep revealing that he's still  mentally a kid but there's no doubt that  from this point on he'll mentally grow  into his body in the important ways  he'll overcome his fear enough to help  luffy reach kaido and he'll get a second  chance to confront kaido in a more manly  way than when kaido spared him all those  years ago and that's only the beginning  and when i say overcome his fear i don't  mean that he'll become fearless just  that he won't be paralyzed by the fear  and will be able to act through it we  then jump to yamato vs kaido a fight  that's been going on longer than i  expected it to each time we catch up  with them it feels like kaido is more  and more in the lead because we  obviously know the strongest creature  will eventually win in a prolonged  battle however yamato doesn't stop  impressing us at first i was like what  is going on when i saw her figure  shatter but it appears to have been a  kind of mirror slash ice clone this got  me off guard because we definitely don't  see something like this in one piece as  much as we do in naruto kaido thinks  this means she's going on the defensive  but then yamato pops out of the  surroundings and lands a very satisfying  hit that brings the yonko down to the  ground not for long but still very  impressive that yamato is doing things  like this after all these chapters not  to take away from yamato's amazing  efforts but we also can't really assume  kaido is going all out as he keeps  trying to convince his child that she  should be on his side you think he'd  give up by now after all these years but  he keeps trying to convince her saying  she acts like she's from wano but can't  escape the truth of her blood she's  kaido's child and the samurai will never  accept her as one of them so even though  they're in the middle of a war and kaido  should probably be finishing her off as  soon as possible here it sounds like  he's being protective in his own messed  up way it's like he doesn't want yamato  to be disappointed and feel left out  because the others won't ever truly  accept her while he will yamato then  tells him to shut up and hits him in the  face saying what's that got to do with  anything for her she's doing the right  thing and it doesn't necessarily matter  if the samurai accept her as a samurai  or not as i said before for a yonko  kaido is being and has been very lenient  towards yamato still a bad dad no doubt  but most military leaders would not have  put up with a constantly defying  presence for two whole decades and after  all this time he's still trying to  reason with yamato in the middle of a  giant war kaido tries to break yamato's  will by saying she's alone which is why  she's been crawling through addicts and  desperately trying to escape wano but  yamato says she's not alone she has and  had friends and she thinks of ace kaido  brings up the samurai from last chapter  including zoro's dad i'm guessing and  says that everyone that shows her  compassion ends up dead now he's trying  to make her feel alone and guilty we get  a flashback where she overheard that  someone was executed because he was  feeding the oni princess and the mental  games might really be getting to yamato  since kaido is able to land a powerful  hit that brings yamato down and at this  point it really feels like kaido starts  projecting aka trying to force his own  view of his experiences onto yamato's  life he's hitting yamato while saying  their acts of kindness were just lies  the truth is they were all afraid of you  after all you could easily use your  power to impose your will on others  you're the offspring of an oni relying  on the friendship of humans is beneath  you we see kaido's monstrous figure and  i don't think he's ever looked so  demented clearly he is a tortured  individual and like i said i feel like  what he's saying reveals more about  himself and how he feels than it does  about yamato in one piece we don't know  much about oni but a quick search lets  us know that in japanese folklore and  oni is a type of demonic creature often  of giant size great strength and fearful  appearance interestingly enough they are  said to be cruel and malicious but they  can be converted to buddhism in other  words even these demonic creatures can  turn over a new leaf if oni really is a  bonafide race in one piece it explains  why kaido and yamato have horns even in  their human forms and this could be an  unofficial translation thing so take it  with a grain of salt but kaido does say  she's the offspring of an oni singular  rather than of multiple oni so she could  even have a human mom from wano who  knows she might be half half in which  case that adds another layer to her  character and struggle either way i look  forward to oda fleshing out the  importance of oni in one piece as we  move forward and we'll hopefully learn  more about their history for instance  does kaido hate the idea of relying on  humans because historically humans  betrayed the oni whatever the case kaido  is clearly a man in pain and tortured by  something then we jump to luffy riding  dragon momo as they make their way  through the sky and towards the island  hilariously momo overcame his fear in  part by closing his eyes so he can't see  how high up they are this leads to such  a funny moment where the giant dragon  breaks through the ceiling of the live  floor and everyone sees luffy riding on  top of a kaido-like dragon how's that  for a morale boost not only is luffy  alive and well he also recruited a  kaido-sized dragon for their team too  that could not have worked out better  momo just keeps crashing through  ceilings and so eventually they'll have  to get to the roof we even get to pass  big mom law and kid i just love to see  the reactions of all the characters big  mom's reaction is hilarious as she  wonders if that's luffy riding kaido and  wonders what's happening luffy keeps  telling momo to open his eyes which is  not surprising when you keep torpedoing  through walls face first what a great  way to shake up the energy in the castle  some people think kaido is wreaking  havoc while others notice that this one  is a different color so there are two  dragons in play kaido for his part  thinks big mom is to blame when he hears  all the damage having no idea that he's  about to see his dragon twin it's funny  how in the distance behind yamato you  suddenly just see momo panting going the  wrong way i really enjoy the humor in  this chapter i gotta say finally they  spot kaido and decide to crash land  there and momo's eyes are finally open  props to him luffy enters gear fourth  snake man my favorite gear form so far  as yamato goes to hit kaido luffy makes  it a combo and they send the yonko  flying back the luffy and yamato reunion  is great and full props to yamato who  not only kept kaido busy but seems  pretty fine even now i half expected her  to be down by the time luffy finally got  there but she's still smiling and able  to land hits truly amazing and oni must  be one of the races with the most  endurance because kaido bounces back in  his dragon form seemingly not a scratch  on him this dude has been fighting  non-stop for a good while with a lot of  top tier opponents and looks completely  fine as if he's just getting warmed up  it's not surprising that even though  he's apparently lost in the past he's  never been killed but we finally see the  two dragons face to face as kaido  wonders how is luffy breathing and who  is this dragon luffy proclaims once  again echoing last time where he did get  overpowered that it doesn't matter what  kaido does luffy is not going to die he  says i'm the man who'll be king of the  pirates then momo has his chance at an  epic reintroduction at first he stutters  but then gets into it and says my name  is kozuki momonosuke i am the man who  will become shogun of wano as he stares  down kaido's dragon form it's a far cry  from his crying self as kaido spared him  20 years ago and i'm really proud to see  how far he's come of course yamato's  eyes brighten up as she recognizes its  momo and i can't wait to see her react  to momo's odin looking adult form she  may well fall in love since they are  pretty much the same physical age right  now and she is odin's biggest fan kaido  laughs saying you're the brat how  unexpected this world doesn't need  another dragon so he clearly remembers  momonosuke and yeah it's clear that he  did not expect him to come back in this  way we're told that i quote head-to-head  clash of dragons and that is it for this  chapter there will be a break next week  but this was definitely an epic chapter  to go on break with luffy vs kaido for  the final time is here we even got to  see a punch thrown we'll get to see how  the two dragon dynamic goes visually  luffy looks like a boss here there are  two dragons present but only one luffy  and he's even riding on top of one of  them as if it's his tamed pet obviously  the actual circumstances are a bit more  complicated but i'm pointing out what  people would visually be seeing and this  is how legends start imagine if luffy  wins how the people who saw him riding a  dragon will speak of him luffy the  dragon tamer so much greatness here as  always let me know what your favorite  moment of the chapter was who was your  mvp this time around i'm torn between  momo and yamato momo faced his fears by  closing his eyes hilariously destroyed  kaido's castle and helped luffy shock  everyone before finally facing kaido and  staring him down as he made his  reintroduction on the other hand yamato  not only kept kaido busy all this time  she was still getting good hits on him  and was still going strong when luffy  came that oni endurance really appears  to be next level also let me know what  you're most looking forward to seeing  next if you did enjoy this video you  know what to do channel the paraking  within and smash that like button with  no mercy remember that smashing is  piraking energy and passing is orochi  energy so the choice is yours if you  haven't make this the video you  subscribe and this is crucial hit that  notification bell to turn on all  notifications or you will miss future  one piece videos and updates that's just  the way it works and while you wait for  the next chapter to drop feel free to  check out my big and growing one piece  playlist that includes videos on all the  yonko warlords admirals and much more  link to tha